# spam_detector_ml.enlg — Spam Email Classifier using EnLang Simplified ML Syntax
# Same model, same accuracy — but now in clean natural English!
# EnLang ML Syntax: load → split → vectorize → train → evaluate → predict

display "============================================================"
display " ENLANG ML SPAM CLASSIFIER (Simplified Natural Syntax) "
display "============================================================"
display ""

# 1. Load dataset with labels
load dataset from "d:/enlangg/examples/spam email labeling/emails.csv" with text column text and label column spam

# 2. Split 80% training, 20% testing
split dataset into 80 percent training and 20 percent testing

# 3. Vectorize text using TF-IDF (max 5000 features)
vectorize text using tfidf with max features 5000

# 4. Train Naive Bayes Classifier
train naive_bayes classifier on training data

# 5. Evaluate Model Accuracy
evaluate classifier accuracy and store in acc

display ""
display "Final Test Accuracy: " + acc + "%"
display ""

# 6. Demo Predictions using simplified syntax
display "============================================================"
display " SAMPLE PREDICTIONS "
display "============================================================"
predict spam from "CONGRATULATIONS! You won a $1,000,000 lottery prize! Click here now!"
predict spam from "Project meeting scheduled for tomorrow at 10 AM in Conference Room B."
predict spam from "Get cheap Viagra and Cialis online! 75% off! Limited time offer!"
predict spam from "Hi team, please review the attached report and send your feedback."
